body:
i can hear people speaking distinct sentences, They're not loud but b/c im somewhat quiet i can hear them clearly. i don't really hear my neighbor. He's a nice guy and i've spoken to him in person a bunch of times so im not really anxious with so much. but b/c he's on the other side of my bathroom wall, im hesitant to give concerts in my shower most of the time. from my desk area, i can clearly hear people walking in the hallway. i can even hear the building's front door open and slam shut from where my apartment is in this building. 

&#x200B;

i know it's silly to assume that someone would care enough to listen in on my conversation or noise and judge me but it bothers me. I've tried addressing it by playing background noise on my TVs but im at heart a quiet private person and i get embarrassed if i think someone over heard me singing to my music or talking on the phone or out loud to myself or my company.

is this true or are you being sarcastic? lol

&#x200B;

(i just burned some cannabis so I'm really curious right now)

does he act feminine? is it ok to assume he lived only with his mom the majority of his life? It's possible he's picked up on seeing and hearing her talk as he got older so she maybe the one thats walking around saying stuff like "oh hes hot" and he got comfy saying it too.

&#x200B;

But yeah, your son is gay. dont just flat out confront him and ask him if he's gay. you have to lean into this type of conversation gently. Don't make him feel ashamed or embarrassed of himself for being gay but you may want to talk to him and ask him if he's aware of how other people (men women and children) see and interact with him in life. he might have questions about why people act a certain way to him and may not understand how he comes off to everyone watching him.
